// Title: Vulnerable software on devices (Defender Vulnerability Management): summary and per device
// Purpose: Which software on managed devices carries the most CVEs, critical CVEs and CVEs with a public exploit.
// Source table(s): DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities, DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilitiesKB (Advanced Hunting)
// Parameters to edit: OsPlatforms.
// Notes/traps: run in the Defender portal, Advanced hunting (these tables are NOT in Log Analytics unless you
//          stream them). IsExploitAvailable comes from the KB table, hence the join. The join is
//          leftouter so software without KB match is kept. Query 2 gives the per device view.
//
// --- Query 1: per software
let OsPlatforms = dynamic(["Windows10", "Windows11"]);
DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities
| where OSPlatform in (OsPlatforms)
| join kind=leftouter (DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilitiesKB | project CveId, CvssScore, IsExploitAvailable) on CveId
| summarize Devices = dcount(DeviceId), CVEs = dcount(CveId),
            CriticalCVEs = dcountif(CveId, VulnerabilitySeverityLevel == "Critical"),
            ExploitCVEs = dcountif(CveId, IsExploitAvailable == true),
            Versions = make_set(SoftwareVersion, 15)
    by SoftwareVendor, SoftwareName
| order by ExploitCVEs desc, Devices desc
//
// --- Query 2: per device and software version (run separately)
// DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities
// | where OSPlatform in ("Windows10", "Windows11")
// | summarize CVEs = dcount(CveId), CriticalCVEs = dcountif(CveId, VulnerabilitySeverityLevel == "Critical")
//     by DeviceName, OSPlatform, SoftwareVendor, SoftwareName, SoftwareVersion
// | order by DeviceName asc, CriticalCVEs desc
